            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45570",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "go-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "go-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4, go-git's SSH transport constructs the remote exec command by wrapping the repository path in single quotes without escaping single quotes embedded inside the path. A repository path containing a single quote can therefore break out of the quoted region in the exec command and be appended as additional shell tokens. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45570",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-45570\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/go-git/go-git/v5\nFixed Version: 5.19.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-45570](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45570)\ngo-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4, go-git's SSH transport constructs the remote exec command by wrapping the repository path in single quotes without escaping single quotes embedded inside the path. A repository path containing a single quote can therefore break out of the quoted region in the exec command and be appended as additional shell tokens. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-45570**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/go-git/go-git/v5|5.19.1|[CVE-2026-45570](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45570)|\n\ngo-git is an extensible git implementation library written in pure Go. Prior to 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4, go-git's SSH transport constructs the remote exec command by wrapping the repository path in single quotes without escaping single quotes embedded inside the path. A repository path containing a single quote can therefore break out of the quoted region in the exec command and be appended as additional shell tokens. This vulnerability is fixed in 5.19.1 and 6.0.0-alpha.4."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.3,
